WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.082
Our NumPy retriever is excellent for learning, but it is not always the right storage layer for a real application.

00:00:10.082 --> 00:00:16.972
With a small dataset, comparing one query vector against every stored vector is easy.

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:25.857
As collections grow, teams usually need persistence, indexing, metadata filters, APIs, concurrent users, backups,

00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:32.787
and operational tooling. That is where vector indexes and vector databases become useful.

00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:37.028
A vector database does not create RAG by itself.

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:42.538
It mainly helps store and search vectors and associated metadata efficiently.

00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:49.113
This distinction matters because people sometimes equate RAG with a particular database product.

00:00:49.113 --> 00:00:54.213
RAG is the architecture. The vector database is one component.

00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:58.843
For a classroom project, NumPy or Chroma may be enough.

00:00:58.843 --> 00:01:06.538
For a production service, you may choose a server-based or managed system depending on scale, security, operations,

00:01:06.538 --> 00:01:09.272
and existing infrastructure.
